  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Minor coastal flooding expected along the coast and \nlower Cape Fear River at least for a few more days, especially \nduring daytime high tides. \n\nHigh astronomical tides along with continued positive tidal \nanomalies will lead to additional minor coastal flooding along the \ncoast and lower Cape Fear River through at least Wed, especially \nduring the daytime high tides. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Temperatures will gradually warm up through the work \nweek with rain chances returning late week. \n\nGeneral troughing over the area will get replaced by high pressure \nlate week leading to a warming and eventual moistening trend toward \nthe end of the work week. High temperatures should climb above \nnormal starting Tuesday and continue into Friday with 90s possible \nonce again inland starting Wed. Overnight lows should stay near to \nbelow normal a few more nights due to the dry air mass and pretty \nfavorable radiational cooling conditions, then climb above normal \nstarting Wed night before falling a bit over the weekend. \n\nRain chances should hold off until Fri when low chances return with \na bit better chances possible over the weekend as a stalling front \napproaches, although confidence remains low regarding rain \nchances/timing/amounts. At least there doesn't appear to be a \nsignificant risk for severe storms or excessive rainfall at this \ntime.",
